d":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T10:22:49-07:00","id":1311009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/BxPRTjkgDXndXnxQ45MNoAY91jlMnCntsPSykw0/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/BxPRTjkgDXndXnxQ45MNoAY91jlMnCntsPSykw0/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/BxPRTjkgDXndXnxQ45MNoAY91jlMnCntsPSykw0/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.instagram.com/p/BxPRTjkgDXndXnxQ45MNoAY91jlMnCntsPSykw0/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:03:51-07:00","id":1311014,"title":"","content":"From the packaging, I assume those are Q-Workshop dice? Are they of similar quality to other Q-Workshop dice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:36:58-07:00","id":1311022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1310443-has-anyone-gotten-their-books-yet?p=1311014#post1311014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the packaging, I assume those are Q-Workshop dice? Are they of similar quality to other Q-Workshop dice?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think I've ever seen Q Workshop dice. I'm not fond of these at all. They seem just basic gray plastic with the graphics printed on them. I'm sure OPP is doing their best but they seem pretty cheap. Nothing like the prototype photos at all. I would suggest contacting a company like Chessex for a special run.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T11:56:45-07:00","id":1311027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>karpomatic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1310443-has-anyone-gotten-their-books-yet?p=1311022#post1311022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think I've ever seen Q Workshop dice. I'm not fond of these at all. They seem just basic gray plastic with the graphics printed on them. I'm sure OPP is doing their best but they seem pretty cheap. Nothing like the prototype photos at all. I would suggest contacting a company like Chessex for a special run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry you don't like them, but they are indeed Q-Workshop dice, the face designs are 3-D, and then the ink filled in the designs. Although the designs are simplified, because there's no way to make the Pantheon symbols in the detail they are in 2D art, they are individualized, in different colors, in grey as per the mock-ups. Chessex would not be able to do these.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T12:17:38-07:00","id":1311030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1310443-has-anyone-gotten-their-books-yet?p=1311027#post1311027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry you don't like them, but they are indeed Q-Workshop dice, the face designs are 3-D, and then the ink filled in the designs. Although the designs are simplified, because there's no way to make the Pantheon symbols in the detail they are in 2D art, they are individualized, in different colors, in grey as per the mock-ups. Chessex would not be able to do these.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's all good, Rich. I'm not here to bash them. You can't please everyone, right? I'm surprised that Chessex can't do it. I guess it's a different process. I'm not sorry I bought them. I'll just leave them sealed and wait 20 years to sell them for a mint on Ebay like the old WOD dice are going for now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T12:54:07-07:00","id":1311038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohanDracys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1310443-has-anyone-gotten-their-books-yet?p=1310933#post1310933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. As incompetent as I am with a computer, I do know how to do that at least. And no, it does not work. It has never worked. None of my surveys have ever shown up, and my email is never recognized as having an account.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had this problem too. Tried my email, every password I would have used. It still said my email and info was wrong. I dealt with it a couple years ago, so I'm not sure if I'm remembering everything correctly.<br /> <br /> At some point I got emails from KS or Backerkit saying &quot;here's your link to your pledge&quot;. If I clicked on the link, I'd see my pledge and modify it on the Backerkit site, but I couldn't log in (as I mentioned) to see my other pledges. Each link like that was separate. It's like the links went directly to the pledge and didn't care if I had an account.<br /> <br /> So to fix it, I started with one of those links. Then I clicked the sign up button in the upper right. I went through registration using the same email address I used with KS and my KS associated surveys (and thus BK). Once I finished that, I want to say there was a link to 'recover my account'. I said yes, and it grabbed all the pledges with my email address attached to them and added them to my account. It's worked since.<br /> <br /> If you don't have one of those links, you might be able to straight up register and recover the pledges that way. No guarantees, tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/753-ariketh","name":"Ariketh","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T15:40:39-07:00","id":1311078,"title":"","content":"Got my copy of the Scion books today! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T16:14:46-07:00","id":1311088,"title":"","content":"Yep. Got mine too.<br /> <br /> The dice are unusual. They're really light, almost like they're hollow? Or made of something different? <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5\" data-vbnamecard=\"5\">RichT</a> can you comment on the composition of the things?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-09T16:44:10-07:00","id":1311096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ariketh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1310443-has-anyone-gotten-their-books-yet?p=1311038#post1311038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I had this problem too. Tried my email, every password I would have used. It still said my email and info was wrong. I dealt with it a couple years ago, so I'm not sure if I'm remembering everything correctly.<br /> <br /> At some point I got emails from KS or Backerkit saying &quot;here's your link to your pledge&quot;. If I clicked on the link, I'd see my pledge and modify it on the Backerkit site, but I couldn't log in (as I mentioned) to see my other pledges. Each link like that was separate. It's like the links went directly to the pledge and didn't care if I had an account.<br /> <br /> So to fix it, I started with one of those links. Then I clicked the sign up button in the upper right. I went through registration using the same email address I used with KS and my KS associated surveys (and thus BK). Once I finished that, I want to say there was a link to 'recover my account'. I said yes, and it grabbed all the pledges with my email address attached to them and added them to my account. It's worked since.<br /> <br /> If you don't have one of those links, you might be able to straight up register and recover the pledges that way. No guarantees, tho.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah except Backerkit objects to AOL. So meh. I have my PDFs, presumably I'll get my books soon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25297-johandracys","name":"JohanDracys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"}